   "evidence": "Distance.lean:203 states `lipschitzOnWith_of_norm_curveVelocity_le` (line 253) under `variable {M : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace M] ... [IsRiemannianManifold I M]`. Rademacher.lean:52 uses `{M : Type*} [PseudoEMetricSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M] [IsManifold I 1 M]`. `LipschitzWith.comp_lipschitzOnWith` and `norm_deriv_le_of_lipschitzOn` (the map `f \u2218 \u03b3 : \u211d \u2192 F`) do not need a metric on `M`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Riemannian/Gradient/Lipschitz.lean",
   "fix": "Replace `[MetricSpace M]` with `[PseudoEMetricSpace M]` in the section variables. The three statements stay the same.",
   "issue": "`[MetricSpace M]` is too strong. The proofs use only `LipschitzWith`/`LipschitzOnWith` composition and `IsRiemannianManifold.lipschitzOnWith_of_norm_curveVelocity_le`, and both work over a pseudo-extended metric. As written, the results exclude the extended Riemannian distance from `EMetricSpace.ofRiemannianMetric` on disconnected manifolds, and they do not line up with Rademacher's theorem, which this file is meant to be paired with.",
